    {
      "id": "pp089qc",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Sutlej is the longest river in HP. It enters HP from Tibet through Shipkila Pass.",
        "Beas originates at Beas Kund (~4000m) near Rohtang Pass.",
        "Gobind Sagar (Bhakra Dam reservoir on Sutlej) – largest man-made lake in HP.",
        "Pong Dam Lake (Maharana Pratap Sagar on Beas, Kangra) – Ramsar wetland site.",
        "Spiti River is the main tributary of Sutlej flowing through the cold desert Spiti Valley.",
        "Baspa River (Baspa Valley / Sangla Valley) joins Sutlej at Tapri, Kinnaur.",
        "Chandra and Bhaga rivers join at Tandi (Lahaul) to form Chenab (Chandrabhaga).",
        "Pandoh Dam (Mandi) diverts Beas water to Gobind Sagar via tunnel.",
        "River Yamuna forms the eastern boundary of HP with Uttarakhand in the Sirmaur area."
      ]
    },
