    {
      "id": "muuyc9w",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<img alt=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/JkUMlvkfOwP_7WVaZeh-msE3k8otJyvZZA9fp9tPOGd50iJlqi3kofvFde4Ys3qjATWwE48CISjBrpTSIa3gPtL9sF03RE58uy4N39uFuJTf4MuGSQYn9_T_pQy6rI0pBgCy7htIxwhdJPKxrRF7guRbmR5yRQNqJPiuxiBo3gK-ZaY7usW9Db5ANfJOH1Uv?purpose=fullsize\" src=\"/books/Guide/Himachal_Pradesh_CONSTABLE/images/image_tal4sql.jpeg\"/>Bara Shigri Glacier: Longest glacier in HP and second longest in India (about 25 km). Located in Lahaul; feeds the Chandra River.",
        "Kulti Glacier: In Lahaul.",
        "Gepang Gath Glacier: In Lahaul-Spiti.",
        "Chandra Glacier: Source of the Chandra River (one branch of Chenab).",
        "Bhaga Glacier (near Surajtal): Source of Bhaga River.",
        "Beas Kund: Source glacier/lake of the Beas River (near Rohtang Pass).",
        "Glaciers are critical for river discharge. Climate change-induced glacial retreat is a major environmental challenge in HP.",
        "HP is studying glacial retreat impacts through HP Climate Change Cell and various research institutions."
      ]
    },
