    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Dharamshala receives about 3400 mm annual rainfall – one of the wettest places in North India. Spiti Valley receives only about 170 mm – cold desert conditions. The difference is due to Dhauladhar acting as a barrier to monsoon clouds.",
      "id": "avmtnmv"
    }
